    "formBuilderImportXlsformNoticeDesc": <div
      style={
        Object {
          "fontSize": 13,
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "textAlign": "left",
        }
      }
    >
      <p
        style={
          Object {
            "margin": "4px 0 8px 0",
            "textAlign": "left",
          }
        }
      >
        Your XLSForm was imported successfully, but Kobo and Akvo MIS don't work identically and some form logic may need manual adjustment to fully match your original. Please review the warnings below and test the form before publishing.
      </p>
      <p
        style={
          Object {
            "fontWeight": 600,
            "margin": "8px 0 4px 0",
            "textAlign": "left",
          }
        }
      >
        Common things to check:
      </p>
      <ul
        style={
          Object {
            "listStyleType": "disc",
            "margin": "0 0 8px 0",
            "paddingLeft": 18,
            "textAlign": "left",
          }
        }
      >
        <li
          style={
            Object {
              "marginBottom": 4,
            }
          }
        >
          Calculated fields – formulas may need to be re-verified
        </li>
        <li
          style={
            Object {
              "marginBottom": 4,
            }
          }
        >
          Dynamic repeat counts – repeat groups driven by a variable may need manual setup
        </li>
        <li
          style={
            Object {
              "marginBottom": 4,
            }
          }
        >
          Group relevance / skip logic – conditional group visibility should be double-checked
        </li>
        <li
          style={
            Object {
              "marginBottom": 4,
            }
          }
        >
          "Other" follow-up questions – these aren't auto-converted; add them manually if needed
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p
        style={
          Object {
            "margin": "8px 0 0 0",
            "textAlign": "left",
          }
        }
      >
        We recommend previewing the full form and testing a submission before it goes live.
      </p>
    </div>,
